# Shared PostgreSQL port/linkage adaptations owned by the main WASIX runtime.
#
# The retired hash, XID, LIKE and B-tree shortcuts (0014, 0015, 0016, 0024,
# 0026) must not survive in this product after removal from the canonical stack.
# The B-tree shortcuts were already inert without OLIPHAUNT_WASM_SINGLE_USER.
# No retained patch depends on those changes.
#
# Concurrent postmaster/backends retain normal spinlocks and atomics; the
# retired single-backend substitutions (0035/0036) never belonged in this lane.
# 0018 fixes tool symbol linkage. 0037 uses getrandom directly in Postmaster,
# without the single-backend entropy reservoir that a fork could duplicate.
0018-oliphaunt-wasix-avoid-pg-dump-executequery-lto-collision.patch
0037-oliphaunt-wasix-use-checked-getrandom.patch
